---
import DocsLayout from "@layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Split Panes" description="Multi-pane editing in Axon">
    <h1>Split Panes</h1>

    <p>
        Axon supports splitting the editor into multiple panes, allowing you to
        view and edit several files side by side. This is essential for
        comparing code, editing related files, or keeping reference
        documentation open while you work.
    </p>

    <h2>Creating Split Panes</h2>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Action</th>
                    <th>macOS</th>
                    <th>Windows/Linux</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Split pane right</td>
                    <td><code>Cmd+\</code></td>
                    <td><code>Ctrl+\</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Split pane down</td>
                    <td><code>Cmd+Shift+\</code></td>
                    <td><code>Ctrl+Shift+\</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Close current pane</td>
                    <td><code>Cmd+W</code></td>
                    <td><code>Ctrl+W</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Focus next pane</td>
                    <td><code>Cmd+1</code>, <code>Cmd+2</code>, etc.</td>
                    <td><code>Ctrl+1</code>, <code>Ctrl+2</code>, etc.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Managing Panes</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Drag tabs</strong> — Move tabs between panes by dragging
        </li>
        <li><strong>Resize panes</strong> — Drag the divider between panes</li>
        <li>
            <strong>Close panes</strong> — Click the X on a tab or use keyboard shortcuts
        </li>
        <li><strong>Up to 4 panes</strong> — Create a 2x2 grid maximum</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Dirty Indicators</h2>
    <p>
        When a file has unsaved changes, a dot appears on the tab. Axon will
        prompt you to save before closing a pane with unsaved files.
    </p>

    <h2>Shared Models</h2>
    <p>
        The same file opened in multiple panes shares a single editor model.
        Changes made in one pane are immediately visible in all panes showing
        that file.
    </p>
</DocsLayout>
